WEBVTT

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:11.440
I'm waiting for the sun, just to say...{fi}

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:11.440
taiyou to machi awase

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:14.490
good morning to a brand new day.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:14.490
ohayou BRAND NEW DAY

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:17.700
Wearing a matching pair of shoelaces,

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:17.700
osoroi no kutsu himo de

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.870
I will run out to my dear boyfriend.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.870
kakedasou DEAR BOY FRIEND

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:24.250
While I'm wearing my uniform,

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:24.250
seifuku ni tsumekonda

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:27.250
a premonition is calling out to me.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:27.250
yokan ga yobu no

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:33.470
I wanted to line up with him in the prism.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:33.470
PURIZUMU ni kasanareba aitai watashi

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:39.970
What does the flower bud think as it starts to grow?

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:39.970
fukurami hajimeta tsubomi wa donna omoi

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:46.730
A tail wind blew from the south, as if winking at me. {link, link}

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:48.770
minami kara fuita oikaze ga UINKU shita

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:53.030
{fad(210,0)}I want to spend more and more sparkling everydays with you.

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:53.030
kirakira no mainichi wo kimi to motto atsumetai ne

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:59.530
We'll find dramatic experiences to make today a better day...

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:59.530
DORAMATIKU mitsumeatte kyou ga motto kagayaku

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:05.960
...and find a more glittering new you.

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:05.960
pikapika no atarashii kimi wo motto mitsuketai na

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:12.090
I want to show a top-class dramatic smile...

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:12.090
DORAMATIKU tobikiri no egao motto agetai

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:18.510
...as I've been invited by the stage where love blooms.

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:18.510
koi saku SUTEEJI ni sasowarete

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:23.640
Ever-thrilling school days, Yeah Yeah!

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:23.640
tokimeki SCHOOL DAYS YEAH-YEAH!

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:29.980
Original TV-Fansub: Ryoumi 
 Encode: Jumonji-Giri 
 Additional Work: ReDone-Subs

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:43.740
<i>Why does it seem so...</i>

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:46.020
<i>...far?</i>

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:48.340
<i>You're so far away from me, Yuuji.</i>

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:06.390
To Yuuji

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:11.400
Living 6

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:11.400
Carried Like a Princess? {may be changed from ep 5}

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:13.440
I'm sorry.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:17.000
It may be a day off, but Kazuki-chan left for club practice.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:21.160
Say, how are things
 between Yuu-chin and Kazuki?

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:25.410
Now that you mention it,
 they haven't seen each other since then.

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:29.170
They go to school and
 eat their meals separately.

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:31.380
It feels so lonely, you know.

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:33.840
As I thought...

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:39.220
I understand. You hate me too, Yuuji.

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:43.330
I won't ever speak with you again. 
Let's break up!

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:44.890
Kazuki!

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.440
What's with you, Yuu-chin?!

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:53.110
Why are you acting so childish? Hurry up and chase her!

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:54.270
Ugh.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:56.630
What are you doing?!

00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:58.400
It's wrong to force them.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:01.910
I can't let poor Yuuji 
take any more damage.

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:04.830
Onee-san, Marie-chin, 
when did you get here?

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:06.830
And what do you mean by "poor Yuuji"?

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:16.170
It seems that the words "break up" 
had a considerable effect on him.

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:19.370
What?! He froze up out of shock?!

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:21.930
Kazuki-chan's in a quandary.

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:25.050
Even though she hates perverts,
 she still likes him.

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:30.150
If Kazuki doesn't hurry up, 
 you might just snag Yuuji-kun for yourself.

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:32.940
Eh? Me? Why should I want Yuu-chin?

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:42.110
Yes, Chihaya-chan.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:45.530
She got the wrong idea and believes I have feelings for Yuu-chin!

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:49.540
"One day trip to the Atsumi hot springs"

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:48.490
Good answer. {rc styles on this section when actually hearing it.}

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:54.020
"If you don't want him, then I'll take him."
Sounds like a declaration of rivalry to <i>me.</i>

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:55.960
I know <i>I'd</i>  be jealous.

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:59.210
Yes, I did say that...

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:01.300
But I didn't really <i>mean</i> it.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:05.010
Wait, how'd you find out about that?

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:07.560
I have my ways.

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:11.520
This is bad, what should I do? {end flashback?}

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:14.600
I've been mulling it over for the past few days,

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:17.820
but I still don't know how to
 broach the subject with them.

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:21.430
Oh, first you stir things up,
 and now you're trying to evade the fallout?

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:26.280
Like I said, I'll be sure to
 talk to them today!

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:28.390
Just kidding.

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:31.040
I don't think you need to blame yourself.

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:35.920
Since you're friends with her,
 it's only natural to get along with Yuuji-kun.

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:39.800
Besides, it was Kazuki-chan who first jumped to the wrong conclusions.

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:45.210
When Yuuji-kun was young, 
we were practically his only playmates.

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:49.810
So, seeing Yuuji-kun getting friendly with other girls has her confused.

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:54.060
I, on the other hand, would've
 eliminated all my rivals immediately.

00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:57.890
Even so, I never planned on stealing Yuu-chin.

00:04:57.890 --> 00:05:01.320
But... what if Yuuji-kun
 is interested in you?

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:07.550
There's no way that would happen. {orange? what?}

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:11.330
3.01 seconds. Kind of a slow reaction...

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:13.620
I'm done.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.330
Oh, I know!

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:18.290
Kazuki just has to realize that I'm not interested in Yuu-chin.

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:19.750
Hmmm.

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:23.250
But love isn't that simple.

00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:26.980
Then I'll have to have you 
take me to your house, Marie-chin.

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:33.310
Huh?

00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:37.560
Yuu-chin? You're in there, right?
 I'm coming in.

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:48.940
<i>He's so depressed...</i>

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:52.280
<i>There's no way he's interested in me.</i>

00:05:55.530 --> 00:05:58.290
Yuu-chin, if this is so traumatizing,

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:00.220
then why don't you go and make up with Kazuki?

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:01.990
K-Kazuki!?

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:05.590
Huh? Chihaya-chan?

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:08.560
Ahem.

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:11.460
W-What's happening with Kazuki?

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:15.810
I was taking a nap just now, 
so I don't know what's going on.

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:20.680
Don't be so stubborn! 
You've obviously been depressed since then.

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:22.570
What are you talking about?

00:06:22.570 --> 00:06:25.940
As you can see, I'm full of energy!

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:33.410
I could totally tell you were faking it. {That's what he said.}

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:35.570
You're wrong.

00:06:35.570 --> 00:06:40.500
Anyway... I'm hungry,
 so I'm gonna go get something to eat.

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:45.240
Yuu-chin! If you keep up that act,
 Kazuki will break up with you for good!

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:52.380
It looks like he responded 
to "break up" again.

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:57.930
That's for sure. But this is solid proof that Yuu-chin is not interested in me.

00:06:58.260 --> 00:07:00.270
The next step is...

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:16.160
Ah, found you.

00:07:16.610 --> 00:07:18.070
Kazuki!

00:07:22.890 --> 00:07:24.170
Chihaya?

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:28.170
I figured you'd be done with your club by now,
 so I came to pick you up.

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:29.560
Yeah.

00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:32.740
Hang on a moment while I go change.

00:07:38.990 --> 00:07:41.780
Eh... ummm... Kazuki...

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:44.610
Sorry about what happened
 the other day!

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:47.940
I shouldn't have tried to play
 matchmaker with you two.

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:52.200
That's all right. I should apologize
 for getting so angry.

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:01.280
Hey, let's sit down for a while.

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:02.160
Okay.

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:11.750
Say...

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:14.380
Do you think I'll be able to make up with Yuuji again?

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:19.180
I just don't want to make things awkward for everyone else.

00:08:20.050 --> 00:08:23.680
<i>That's a surprise. I was sure she'd be
 more stubborn about that.</i>

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:28.440
<i>But, if I tell her that Yuu-chin isn't interested in me...</i>

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:30.770
However, I don't think it'll work out.

00:08:30.770 --> 00:08:32.190
Huh? Why's that?

00:08:32.730 --> 00:08:34.660
You see, Yuuji...

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:37.910
...said he hated me.

00:08:59.790 --> 00:09:02.840
It's impossible because he hates me now.

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:08.440
Girls like you are probably Yuuji's type.

00:09:08.890 --> 00:09:11.930
It looks hopeless for me.
Ever since I was a kid,

00:09:11.930 --> 00:09:15.610
I've never been able to smile well
 in front of Yuuji.

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:16.450
Smile?

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:22.530
I browsed through 
some old photos this morning.

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:27.710
And I noticed that I wasn't smiling in any of them,

00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:32.210
even though I was with my beloved Yuuji.

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:35.220
I should've been uncontrollably happy.

00:09:35.710 --> 00:09:37.880
Yet I couldn't smile.

00:09:37.880 --> 00:09:40.370
I wanted to, but I couldn't.

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:46.920
Nobody likes a girl that's not cute at all.

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:49.270
So it's only natural that he'd hate me.

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:50.940
Kazuki...

00:09:51.390 --> 00:09:54.580
B-But it's all right.

00:09:55.060 --> 00:09:57.200
I don't care that Yuuji hates me.

00:09:57.860 --> 00:10:00.960
I'm completely fine with that.

00:10:01.610 --> 00:10:02.880
I really don't care.

00:10:06.880 --> 00:10:10.310
If that's so, then why are you crying now?

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:18.960
Have you calmed down?

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:19.790
Yeah...

00:10:20.150 --> 00:10:21.470
Sorry.

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:26.940
No doubt about it, I want you 
and Yuu-chin to get along again.

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:27.970
But...

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:33.480
Why don't you try to meet Yuu-chin halfway?

00:10:35.540 --> 00:10:38.160
You're too hung up on
 your memories of the past.

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:42.310
The present-day Yuu-chin has some charm of his own.

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:45.200
If you don't notice them, 
 you're missing out.

00:10:46.570 --> 00:10:48.960
I think... I noticed.

00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:51.970
He's grown taller.

00:10:51.970 --> 00:10:54.290
We were almost 
the same height back then.

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:57.010
Also, his face looks more mature now.

00:10:57.390 --> 00:10:59.600
I see... So what about his inner strengths?

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:02.720
I can't really understand him.

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:08.180
He's irritating, simple-minded,
 and worst of all, perverted.

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:14.060
Honestly, I was really disappointed that he'd turned out like that.

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:20.030
But... sometimes I see his gentler side,
 and he even has a proper hobby.

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:23.450
I was impressed that he was able to do something so seriously.

00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:26.580
But then he just <i>had</i> to go and molest me again.

00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:35.320
He's just been stringing
 me along all this time.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:36.960
But...

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:38.210
But what?

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:42.070
I am happy that we've met again.

00:11:42.070 --> 00:11:43.470
I think.

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:48.670
I see.

00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:56.140
So, what're you planning to do?

00:11:56.140 --> 00:11:57.060
Huh?

00:11:57.060 --> 00:12:00.490
When all's said and done, 
we <i>are</i> childhood friends.

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:02.980
Being hated makes me sad.

00:12:02.980 --> 00:12:04.940
Still, it was pretty mean for him to say,

00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:07.560
"Without you around, 
we might have some fun for a change."

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:10.200
You still want to quarrel with him?

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:14.510
Now that you're feeling better, 
 I've got something to say.

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:17.840
For the sake of patching things up
 between you two,

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:20.030
I was going to say that I wasn't interested in Yuu-chin.

00:12:20.030 --> 00:12:22.760
So you can relax,
 and not worry about me.

00:12:24.380 --> 00:12:28.930
But I'd be lying if I said I had no interest in him at all.

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:33.370
Chihaya...

00:12:33.760 --> 00:12:34.880
So why-?

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:38.640
Don't get hung up on that!

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:41.270
If you don't want me taking him,
 you'd better work on keeping him!

00:12:41.980 --> 00:12:43.950
Come on, let's go home.

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:51.660
Kazuki!

00:12:52.070 --> 00:12:53.460
Coming!

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:03.510
Chihaya,

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:03.880
Chihaya,

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:05.840
can't we just do this tomorrow?

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:08.170
Stop complaining.

00:13:08.170 --> 00:13:11.010
We should get this out of the way, 
 before you change your mind.

00:13:12.550 --> 00:13:15.270
Let's see how Yuu-chin's doing.

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:16.270
Okay.

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:25.030
O-Onee-chan?

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:40.000
Wait a second, Chihaya! 
Why is Hatsune in Yuuji's room?!

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:42.000
I don't know, I don't know!

00:13:43.100 --> 00:13:46.470
I requested that she come here.

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:50.180
Oh my, is there anyone outside?

00:13:51.880 --> 00:13:53.470
Meoow~

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:55.430
Oh, it's just a cat. {maybe just offscreen}

00:13:57.310 --> 00:13:59.590
Marie-chin, why'd you ask her to do that?

00:13:59.920 --> 00:14:04.440
I asked Hatsune-san to persuade my brother to make up with Kazuki-san.

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:10.160
Hatsune-oneesama also said she didn't want to see him looking so lifeless.

00:14:10.930 --> 00:14:13.030
So that's why...

00:14:13.030 --> 00:14:14.620
What do you mean, "lifeless"?

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:17.490
Poor lost sheep, come here and...

00:14:17.490 --> 00:14:19.880
...tell me all your worries.

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:25.380
L-Like I said, I don't understand what you're talking about.

00:14:25.380 --> 00:14:28.560
You should share your troubles, 
rather than keeping everything to yourself.

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:30.380
I'll even pamper you.

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:36.850
<i>What are you getting so lovestruck about?!</i>

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:39.750
Huh?

00:14:39.750 --> 00:14:43.100
It's okay. I really don't have any worries.

00:14:43.100 --> 00:14:44.400
Are you sure?

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:48.820
I wonder if Kazuki-chan came back?

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:50.820
Uh-oh, she's coming this way.

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:52.570
What do we do <i>now?</i>

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:54.820
Ah!

00:14:54.820 --> 00:14:56.490
She's back.

00:14:58.990 --> 00:15:00.500
So, shall we go?

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:02.710
Why do I have to come along?

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:08.200
Because, it makes me sad 
to see you two quarreling.

00:15:08.490 --> 00:15:12.390
Well, Kazuki and her anger management issues can't get over that incident.

00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:14.550
What incident?

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:18.350
It happened when I was trying to photograph Kazuki.

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:21.020
I guess I did tease her too much,

00:15:21.640 --> 00:15:24.810
so this <i>is</i> partially my fault.

00:15:26.020 --> 00:15:29.310
But I never thought she'd
 take things out on Chihaya-chan.

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:34.000
Then I got all worked up and said...

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:36.450
...that I hated her.

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:37.740
Oh my...

00:15:38.460 --> 00:15:39.730
And then...

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:43.330
I won't ever speak with you again. 
Let's break up!

00:15:44.430 --> 00:15:45.800
What happened?

00:15:46.830 --> 00:15:47.890
Nothing...

00:15:47.890 --> 00:15:51.880
I felt uncomfortable around Kazuki, 
 so I started avoiding her.

00:15:52.670 --> 00:15:57.550
Chihaya, Yuuji will understand things
 if I apologize, won't he?

00:15:57.550 --> 00:16:00.050
Sure he will. I'm telling you,
 everything will turn out okay.

00:16:00.050 --> 00:16:03.130
But still, why is Kazuki always like that?

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:05.180
Like what?

00:16:05.180 --> 00:16:09.650
Unsociable, irritable, and always gloomy.

00:16:09.650 --> 00:16:10.860
What's with her?

00:16:12.410 --> 00:16:15.850
The answer to all his questions
 is in the mirror!

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:20.120
Kitty-cat, where are you?

00:16:20.670 --> 00:16:23.500
Mew~ Meow~

00:16:23.970 --> 00:16:25.420
Now I get it.

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:30.420
So that's how you think of Kazuki-chan.

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:34.520
I've always seen her as a cute,
 charming girl.

00:16:34.810 --> 00:16:39.180
Yeah, but she actually <i>likes</i> you.

00:16:39.660 --> 00:16:42.880
I'm pretty sure I fall on 
the other end of the spectrum.

00:16:44.100 --> 00:16:45.730
Why is that?

00:16:47.210 --> 00:16:48.720
Because of this.

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:50.940
Oh my.

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:52.940
I took it back then.

00:16:52.940 --> 00:16:57.660
<i>Aah! Why does he still have
one of the photos from that day?!</i>

00:16:57.660 --> 00:17:02.000
Kazuki, you're going to blow our cover!

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:04.580
Please keep this a secret from Kazuki.

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:08.170
I really should've erased it,
 but I just couldn't.

00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:13.000
She's always showing me that face,
 and never her real smile.

00:17:13.270 --> 00:17:15.720
There's no way she could ever like me.

00:17:21.090 --> 00:17:24.970
But I've seen Kazuki-chan 
make this expression plenty of times.

00:17:24.970 --> 00:17:27.650
Eh!? Y-You have?

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:31.360
This is how she always looks 
whenever we're fighting.

00:17:32.020 --> 00:17:34.610
You and Kazuki have fights, Hatsune-san?

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:37.860
It's only natural for sisters to quarrel once in a while.

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:42.160
But because she's forgiving, 
 she makes faces like that. {stole this line from manga}

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:44.910
Your situation is no different.

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:50.120
Sure, they say that a smile
 makes a girl look her best.

00:17:50.120 --> 00:17:54.630
But doesn't this expression of hers have its own special charm?

00:17:56.760 --> 00:18:00.510
If it didn't, why would you still have this photo?

00:18:01.010 --> 00:18:03.520
Didn't you say you should erase it?

00:18:05.010 --> 00:18:08.480
Oh, I see now. This is the real Kazuki.

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:12.720
In all the time I've spent with her,
 she's never faked anything.

00:18:12.720 --> 00:18:15.970
It may not be a smile, 
but it's authentically Kazuki.

00:18:16.440 --> 00:18:19.160
Maybe I couldn't erase it
 because it's her true face.

00:18:20.570 --> 00:18:22.100
Yes, it is.

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:27.240
But I think she'd look great if she smiled,
 so I wish she would.

00:18:27.240 --> 00:18:30.330
And now that we've finally been reunited,

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:33.090
I had hoped that we could live and smile together.

00:18:33.090 --> 00:18:34.210
Yuuji...

00:18:35.590 --> 00:18:36.590
Kazuki!

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:54.690
Ah... I was saved, but how?

00:18:55.980 --> 00:18:58.860
Oh my, you're carrying her like a princess!

00:18:58.860 --> 00:19:01.860
Why did you fall from up there, Kazuki?!

00:19:02.360 --> 00:19:04.360
Put me down!

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:08.780
Sorry, Yuu-chin. We heard everything.

00:19:08.780 --> 00:19:12.230
Wait, did you know they were
 up there, Hatsune-san?! {Don't tell me that Hatsune-san knew this?!}

00:19:12.230 --> 00:19:15.660
Nope, I had absolutely no idea.

00:19:15.660 --> 00:19:18.630
We didn't really mean to eavesdrop.

00:19:18.890 --> 00:19:20.130
However...

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:23.800
Erased

00:19:23.800 --> 00:19:26.580
What'd you do that for, Kazuki!?

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:30.600
I can't stand to look 
worse than everyone else.

00:19:31.180 --> 00:19:35.100
If you're going to photograph me,
 I want to be smiling.

00:19:35.810 --> 00:19:37.610
Will you take another one?

00:19:39.770 --> 00:19:41.580
I'm sorry for everything.

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:44.700
I don't really hate you all that much.

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:47.320
W-Well, if you insist...

00:19:47.320 --> 00:19:50.460
Anyway, you were the one who
 started this mess, so from now on...

00:19:55.290 --> 00:19:59.570
Then again, I guess I took things too far
 when I said I hated you.

00:19:59.570 --> 00:20:03.050
I'll be more careful from now on. 
 So, let's get along again.

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:07.180
"Congratulations on your reconciliation!"

00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:08.010
Congratulations on your reconciliation! {+sign saying the same thing?}

00:20:08.010 --> 00:20:08.680
Congratulations on your reconciliation! {+sign saying the same thing?}

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:16.770
What connects your thighs and calves?{One plus one equals?}

00:20:17.230 --> 00:20:18.530
Knees... {Two...}

00:20:21.480 --> 00:20:22.700
Quit clowning around!

00:20:23.070 --> 00:20:25.700
I can't help it; I'm nervous!

00:20:25.990 --> 00:20:30.980
Yuuji-kun, it's a photographer's job to make his models feel at ease.

00:20:30.980 --> 00:20:35.720
If you didn't fail so hard, maybe Kazuki's expression would be more natural!

00:20:36.580 --> 00:20:38.250
Do your best, Onii-chan.

00:20:38.540 --> 00:20:43.540
It's a simple matter of praising her
 and making her feel good.

00:20:43.540 --> 00:20:44.890
Oh, I see.

00:20:44.890 --> 00:20:46.010
Good!

00:20:46.420 --> 00:20:50.220
Hey, Kazuki. I know you tend to act unsociable...

00:20:50.470 --> 00:20:52.770
...but smiling is a very
 important part of being a girl.

00:20:52.770 --> 00:20:53.600
...but smiling is a very
 important part of being a girl.

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:58.390
<i>I also wanted to live and get along with Yuuji...</i>

00:20:58.390 --> 00:20:59.730
<i>...with a smile.</i>

00:21:09.530 --> 00:21:11.200
Ka-Ka-Kawaii (cute)... like a kawauso (otter)!

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:12.830
You mean sea otter.

00:21:13.540 --> 00:21:14.870
Hehe, you're right.

00:21:15.300 --> 00:21:18.380
<i>K-Kawauso!? I'm like a kawauso?!!</i>

00:21:18.680 --> 00:21:21.830
If you like smiles that much, 
 why didn't you take the shot?

00:21:21.830 --> 00:21:23.460
It was very good.

00:21:23.460 --> 00:21:25.170
She looked wonderful.

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:28.170
No, she's like a kawasemi (kingerfish)!

00:21:28.170 --> 00:21:29.630
No... no, she's kawakikitteru (drying up)!

00:21:29.630 --> 00:21:31.950
No, kawaisou (pitiable)!

00:21:31.950 --> 00:21:34.030
Ah, good! Kawaisou!

00:21:33.570 --> 00:21:35.260
Stop it!

00:21:35.260 --> 00:21:38.820
What's the matter with you?
 Are you that hell-bent on pissing me off?!

00:21:38.820 --> 00:21:41.860
Shut up, I don't understand my reactions either.

00:21:42.260 --> 00:21:44.770
And here they'd finally made peace...

00:21:44.770 --> 00:21:46.610
More like war.

00:21:46.610 --> 00:21:47.760
Really?

00:21:48.360 --> 00:21:49.320
So, how about this!?

00:21:49.320 --> 00:21:50.220
So, how about this!?

00:21:49.820 --> 00:21:51.260
No~!

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:58.290
Those two are truly
a match made in heaven.

